How do you design a multi-stage Dockerfile for a Java / Python app?


  Why Multi-Stage Builds?

        A build environment requires:

        Maven/Gradle for Java

        pip, gcc, build-essential for Python

        Compilers and development libraries

    These are needed only during build time, not at runtime.

  Without multi-stage builds:

    Java + Maven + JDK + Source Code + Build Cache + Application

  Result:

    4 GB image

  With multi-stage builds:

    Builder Image
    ↓
    Compile
    ↓
    Copy artifact
    ↓
    Runtime Image

  Result:

    200 MB image



Java Multi-Stage Dockerfile (Spring Boot)


    # Stage 1: Build

    FROM maven:3.9-eclipse-temurin-21 AS builder

    WORKDIR /app

    COPY pom.xml .

    COPY src ./src

    RUN mvn clean package -DskipTests


    # Stage 2: Runtime

    FROM eclipse-temurin:21-jre

    WORKDIR /app

    COPY --from=builder \
         /app/target/app.jar \
         app.jar

    EXPOSE 8080

    ENTRYPOINT ["java","-jar","app.jar"]




Build Flow:-


  Source Code
       ↓
   Maven Build
       ↓
   app.jar
       ↓
  Copy only JAR
       ↓
  JRE Runtime Image

